.TH GIT-DIFF-HTML 1 "2026-09-20" "git-diff-html" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git-diff-html \- render a revision's html file and the working copy side by side, with a word-level diff
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git diff-html
[<revision>] [\-\-] <path>
.br
.B git diff-html
\-\-cleanup | \-C
.SH DESCRIPTION
Renders
.I revision
's version of
.I path
(default revision: HEAD) and the working copy's version side by side in a
web browser, plus a third pane showing a word-level diff (insertions in
green, deletions in red). Display only; nothing can be edited from the
generated page.
.PP
.I path
is resolved like any git pathspec: relative to the current directory, not
necessarily the repository's toplevel.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-cleanup, \-C
Remove every temporary file this command has generated
(\fB$TMPDIR\fR/git\-diff\-html\-*.html, or \fB/tmp\fR if
.B $TMPDIR
is unset) instead of comparing anything. Prints nothing when there was
nothing to remove.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show a short usage summary. (Note: when invoked as
.B git diff-html --help ,
git itself intercepts \fB\-\-help\fR and shows this manual page instead of
running the command; run \fBgit-diff-html -h\fR directly to see the short
usage form.)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
git diff-html \-\- Documentation-ja/git.info
Compare HEAD's version of the file against the working copy.
.TP
git diff-html HEAD~3 \-\- Documentation-ja/git.info
Compare the version from 3 commits ago against the working copy.
.TP
git diff-html \-\-cleanup
Remove leftover generated temporary files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1)
